3
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,000
After extensive study, it's been determined that the chance of precipitation increases

4
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,000
in inverse proportion to the proximity of rain year.

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Research also shows that there's a direct relationship between the probability of precipitation

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:46,000
and the number of moisture-sensitive items exposed to the elements.

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Statistics indicate that the probability these items will be put away before precipitation begins

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000
is in inverse proportion to their monetary value.

9
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Researchers have published a statistical table called the picnic table

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:11,000
and, in practical terms, a loaf of bread left on a picnic table increases the probability

11
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,000
of precipitation by 20%,

12
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:22,000
While a digital camera left on the same table increases the probability of precipitation

13
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,000
by 60%.

14
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,000
I'm Dean Amader.

15
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Thank you for this.

16
