357
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
They were always chasing them down

358
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,000
and trying to figure out where they were

359
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,000
and making them be part of the patrol.

360
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,000
The next senior patrol leader decided

361
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,000
that if these guys wanted to be together

362
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,000
it was going to be useless to fight with them,

363
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,000
so we let them form their own patrol.

364
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,000
Our scouts wanted to be in that patrol,

365
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,000
so for a few months there we had a patrol

366
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
of three scouts.

367
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Once these three friends were together,

368
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
they all showed up at just about

369
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
every meeting and every camp out,

370
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,000
and soon they grew

371
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
from being the terrible trio

372
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:16,000
to becoming a competent, well-behaved patrol.

373
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,000
When it comes to patrols,

374
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,000
let the scouts choose,

375
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,000
accept their choices

376
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,000
and help them solve any problems

377
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,000
that their choices might create.

378
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:28,000
What's not nice and neat?

379
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,000
but scouting is about

380
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,000
the processes involved

381
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:34,000
in making choices

382
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,000
and the alchemy of working together

383
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
with your peers to meet challenges

384
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,000
and solve problems.

385
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:42,000
Talk to your senior patrol leader,

386
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,000
ask him some questions.

387
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,000
ask him if he thinks the patrols

388
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,000
are set up the right way

389
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,000
or if he would change anything.

390
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,000
how is he going to incorporate

391
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:54,000
the new scouts that are coming into the troop,

392
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,000
as he's going to make.

393
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:58,000
you may end up with patrols of 10 or 12,

394
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,000
or patrols of 3 and 4

395
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,000
and everything in between.

396
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,000
you may have patrols with mixed ages

397
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,000
or all the same age.

398
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,000
it may look efficient or messy

399
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:10,000
and you'll wonder if it's a mistake.

400
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,000
but be patient,

401
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,000
work with the patrol leaders council

402
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,000
and watch what happens.

403
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,000
it'll take some practice and some patience,

404
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:20,000
but soon you'll see that those patrols

405
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,000
are full of happy, advancing scouts

406
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:24,000
having the time of their lives.

407
